# Everything the build context does not need. Two entries here are not about speed:
#
# - `.ps/` holds the session cookie and the /watch token. A build context is copied into
#   the daemon and anything COPYed lands in an image layer, where `docker history` can
#   read it back out of a published image. It must never be in the context at all.
# - `.git/` carries every credential that was ever committed and then removed.
.ps/
.git/

# Build outputs — the image builds its own, and a host-built `build/` for another
# architecture would silently shadow it.
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
out/

# Never read by the build.
.github/
.githooks/
.harness/
.idea/
.vscode/
docs/
template/
*.md
.DS_Store
